 redirect via unvalidated returnToUrl\n\nValidate the \\\returnToUrl\\ query parameter before navigating post-login.\nAccept only same-origin URLs whose pathname falls under the configured SPA\nbase path, rejecting external hosts, protocol-relative URLs, and paths\noutside the SPA root.\n\n- Export \\isSafeReturnUrl\\ helper that parses and validates redirect targets\n- Replace unguarded \\\returnToUrl !== '/'\\ check with \\isSafeReturnUrl\\ guard\n- Fall back to \\config.links.loginSuccess\\ when the URL is rejected\n- Add 8 unit tests for \\isSafeReturnUrl\\ covering known attack vectors\n- Add 3 integration tests for open-redirect protection in the component\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): simplify spa base trim in return URL check\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): block open-redirect via unvalidated referrer state in login\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): block open-redirect via unvalidated referrer in location picker\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): encode returnToUrl pathname to prevent query string truncation\n\n* test(esm-login-app): use static encoded string in change-location-link test\n\nUse a hardcoded pre-computed encoded URL string instead of calling\nencodeURIComponent() inside the test assertion. This ensures the test\nactually verifies the production output rather than tautologically\ncomparing the same function call on both sides.\n\n* fix(esm-login-app): prefer node:path over path in vitest.config.ts\n\n* (fix) Allow any same-origin returnToUrl, not just SPA base paths\n\nRemoves the overly restrictive spaBase path check from isSafeReturnUrl.\nSame-origin matching is sufficient to prevent open-redirect attacks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"omeri innocent","authorEmail":"innocentomeri08@gmail.com"},{"hash":"0a053ef44442e145cb520405936f84141ea2d000",